[1mCOMMANDS[0m
       If  you  type  and  send a message that starts with a
       slash ([1m/[22m), it will instead be interpreted as  a  com‐
       mand:

           /[4mname[24m argument1 argument2...

       [4mname[24m is matched case-insensitively.  It can be one of
       the following:

       [1mHELP [22m[search]
           Show  the  list  of  command  (or a commands that
           match the given search terms).

       [1mJOIN [22m<channel>
           Join the given channel.

       [1mPART [22m[channel] [reason]
           Part the given channel, defaults to  the  current
           one if omitted.

       [1mQUIT [22m[reason]
           Quits senpai.

       [1mMOTD[0m
           Show the message of the day (MOTD).

       [1mNAMES[0m
           Show  the  member  list  of  the current channel.
           Powerlevels (such as [4m@[24m for "operator", or  [4m+[24m  for
           "voice") are shown in green.

       [1mTOPIC [22m[topic]
           If  [4mtopic[24m  is omitted, show the topic of the cur‐
           rent channel and, if available,  the  person  who
           set it and the time when it has been set.

           Otherwise,  change the topic of the current chan‐
           nel to [4mtopic[24m.

       [1mMUTE[0m
           Mute the current  channel.  This  prevents  being
           distracted from new messages on unimportant chan‐
           nels.

           This  moves the channel to the end of the server,
           and greys its name out so that  new  messages  do
           not change its color in the list. Highlights will
           still send a notification.

       [1mUNMUTE[0m
           Unmute the current channel. See [1mMUTE[22m.

       [1mPIN[0m
           Pin  the  current channel. This moves the channel
           to the start of the buffer list.

       [1mUNPIN[0m
           Unpin the current channel. See [1mPIN[22m.

       [1mMSG [22m<target> <content>
           Send [4mcontent[24m to [4mtarget[24m.

       [1mREPLY [22m<content>
           Reply to the last person who sent a private  mes‐
           sage.

       [1mME [22m<content>
           Send  a  message  prefixed with your nick (a user
           action). If sent from home,  reply  to  the  last
           person who sent a private message.

       [1mNP[0m
           Send the current song that is being played on the
           system. Uses DBus/MPRIS internally.

       [1mUPLOAD [22m<file path>
           Upload a local file to the bouncer.

       [1mQUOTE [22m<raw message>
           Send [4mraw[24m [4mmessage[24m verbatim.

       [1mLIST [22m[pattern]
           List  public  channels,  optionally  matching the
           specified pattern.

       [1mBUFFER [22m<index|name>
           Switch to the buffer at the  [4mindex[24m  position,  or
           containing [4mname[24m. The buffer list will be filtered
           according  to  the passed name; entering the com‐
           mand will select the first buffer in the list.

       [1mWHOIS [22m<nickname>
           Get information about someone who is connected.

       [1mWHOWAS [22m<nickname>
           Get information  about  someone  who  is  discon‐
           nected.

       [1mNICK [22m<nickname>
           Change your nickname.

       [1mOPER [22m<username> <password>
           Log in to an operator account.

       [1mMODE [22m<nick/channel> <flags> [args]
           Change channel or user modes.

       [1mINVITE [22m<nick> [channel]
           Invite  [4mnick[24m  to  [4mchannel[24m (the current channel if
           not given).

       [1mKICK [22m<nick> [channel] [message]
           Eject [4mnick[24m from [4mchannel[24m (the current  channel  if
           not given) with an optional kick message/reason.

       [1mBAN [22m<nick> [channel]
           Ban [4mnick[24m from entering [4mchannel[24m (the current chan‐
           nel if not given).

       [1mUNBAN [22m<nick> [channel]
           Allow  [4mnick[24m  to  enter [4mchannel[24m again (the current
           channel if not given).

       [1mSEARCH [22m<text>
